<title>HONG KONG: Trade in Shenzhen Int'l shrs suspended.</title>
<headline>Trade in Shenzhen Int'l shrs suspended.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading in shares of opticals products maker Shenzhen International Holdings Ltd was suspended in the afternoon at the company's request pending an announcement, the Hong Kong stock exchange said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The company shares rose to HK$0.16 or 10.32 percent to HK$1.71 at midday. Volume was 242.57 million shares worth HK$410.41 million.</p>
<p>Shenzhen International said earlier on Tuesday that it was in talks to buy an equity interest of a company in China and a property in Shenzhen from the company's 56.6 percent controlling shareholder Shenzhen Building Materials Industrial Group Co.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
